@*
    StarRating.razor
    Purpose: Read-only star rating display with an optional rating count.

    REQ-UI-048 — rebuilt over TrBlazeUI's <Rating> component. The public parameter
    API (Value, RatingCount) is unchanged because PostCard and SearchResults bind to it.

    Dependencies: TrBlazeUI Rating
    Usage: Used in PostCard, PostView, SearchResults for displaying post ratings
*@

@*
    [REQ-NFR-007] 2026-08-11 — TR-045/052 are closed in TrBlazeUI 2.0.2: a `ReadOnly` rating
    renders `role="img"` with an `aria-label`, its stars `aria-hidden`, no radio semantics and no
    tab stop at all. The wrapper `<span aria-hidden data-a11y-decorative>` this component used to
    need — and with it the last dependency on App.razor's deleted MutationObserver — is gone;
    `Rating` splats its own attributes now (TR-030/048).

    The stars stay hidden from assistive technology, but for a different and now honest reason:
    the `sr-only` line beside them says the same thing INCLUDING the rating count, which the
    graphic cannot carry, and announcing both would read the value twice. This is a decorative
    duplicate of adjacent text, not a broken control being papered over.
*@
<div class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5" data-testid="star-rating">
    <Rating Value="@Value"
            Max="5"
            ReadOnly="true"
            AllowHalf="false"
            Size="RatingSize.Small"
            aria-hidden="true" />
    <span class="sr-only" data-testid="star-rating-text">
        Rated @Value out of 5@(RatingCount > 0 ? $" from {RatingCount} ratings" : string.Empty)
    </span>
    @if (RatingCount > 0)
    {
        <span aria-hidden="true" class="text-xs text-muted-foreground" data-testid="total-rating-value">(@RatingCount)</span>
    }
</div>

@code {
    /// <summary>
    /// The rating value, 0-5 stars filled.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter]
    public int Value { get; set; } = 0;

    /// <summary>
    /// Optional count of ratings to display in parentheses. Hidden when zero.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter]
    public int RatingCount { get; set; } = 0;
}
